%% Sequence: the construction scout. Build time: code computes the scenario from open data
%% and Gemini's image model draws the steps. Run time: a planner asks; the scout explains
%% the precomputed scenario and cites only what the documents say.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as lenses/construction<br/>(build scripts)
  participant O as Open data<br/>ROW · OSM · NRCan
  participant I as Gemini<br/>image model
  participant F as data/lenses +<br/>data/renders
  actor P as Planner
  participant S as Server
  participant L as Lead
  participant C as Construction<br/>scout
  participant G as Gemini API
  participant T as Tools
  participant V as Checker
  participant Log as Log

  rect rgb(246, 246, 250)
    Note over B,F: Build time, run once by a developer (no resident data)
    B->>I: render.ts: one prompt per step (cap US$1.50)
    I-->>B: images
    B->>F: JPEGs + prompts and model (construction-renders.json)
    B->>O: ION Stage 2 line and stations, OSM land and roads, ground levels
    O-->>B: GeoJSON, elevations
    B->>B: scout.ts: candidate sites scored 0 to 100<br/>(area 25, line 25, buffer 20, road 15, land 15)
    B->>B: layout.ts: twin 6.5 m bores, cross-passages ≤ 244 m (NFPA 130),<br/>boreholes ~75 m, ≥ 1.5 D below invert (FHWA-NHI-10-034)
    B->>B: steps.ts: 7 steps, durations, noise by-law hours, trucks
    B->>F: construction-row-2027-budget.json<br/>(each step links /api/renders/file)
  end

  rect rgb(255, 255, 255)
    Note over P,Log: Run time
    P->>S: POST /api/decisions/:id/ask<br/>"Where would the tunnel machine start?"
    S->>L: run (after cache and limit checks)
    L->>G: plan
    G-->>L: hand to construction-scout
    L->>C: sub-question
    C->>G: next action
    G-->>C: call construction_sites
    C->>T: construction_sites
    T->>F: read the precomputed lens
    T-->>C: ranked sites, bores, boreholes,<br/>steps, limits (computed, no page)
    C->>T: search_pages / read_page ("68030 RT to Cambridge")
    C->>T: record_statement (budget line, quote on p. 43)
    T->>V: quote on its page? numbers in the quote?
    V-->>T: verified
    T->>Log: statement.recorded
    C->>T: record_computed_figure (site score, method)
    T->>T: the number must appear in the lens<br/>result this run looked up, else rejected
    C->>T: record_tradeoff, record_unknown<br/>(soil, utilities, owners: who can answer)
    C-->>L: verified statements + computed figures
    L-->>P: answer (SSE): "This is an illustrative scenario,<br/>not a Region plan..." with citations
    P->>S: Construction tab: GET /api/decisions/:id, GET /api/renders/:file
    S-->>P: sites on the map, profile, 7 steps,<br/>renders labelled "illustrative"
  end
  Note over P,Log: In a brief draft, these statements go to staff review like any other (see seq-brief). The scout never picks a site.
